<http://data.silknow.org/object/b13372c2-8e2d-315d-a5bb-d91340722d3a>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Execution scene (Mary Queen of Scots?) Three men and three women in 16th century style dress. One woman is kneeling before the block, holding a cross to her chest, while the other two console her. The men, one seated, one holding a headsman's axe, look on. Country setting. Polychrome floss silk and chenille yarns purl and spangles over a silk (?) ground. Sky, heads and hands of the figures are painted directly onto the ground. Paint cracked and missing in areas. Mounted on a board."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/82a0bbd7-eee5-3497-b9a6-aab696acc931> ;
